 "about": "Real roughness (how matte a surface is; 0 = mirror, 1 = chalk) by material name, first match wins (case-insensitive, part of the name). Many models were made glossier than real things (a parquet floor at 0.07 is a mirror). tools/albedo_audit.py writes each material's least roughness into assets/models/albedo.json ('rough'); the new lighting never draws a material smoother than that. 0 = left as made (glass, liquids, screens, glowing parts). Sources: measured roughness in physically based material tables (physicallybased.info) and photos of the real things.",
